2‑Dodecylphenol (2‑DDP) is an alkylphenol in which a twelve‑carbon dodecyl chain is ortho‑positioned on the phenolic ring. It serves as a versatile intermediate for oil‑soluble phenolic resins, antioxidants, lubricant additives, surfactants and epoxy curing agents, with prominent applications in fuel additives, rubber chemicals, coatings and specialty resins.
